{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest","id":879761,"title":"Question Regarding Alien Allure and Be My Guest","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-01T16:45:44-07:00","id":879761,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Question Regarding Alien Allure and Be My Guest","content":"With Alien Allure's Normal effect, how far does it go?<br /> <br /> It indicates that (aside from Heroes) one can harm someone and yet the next day receive a Good Impression, and &quot;all is forgiven.&quot;<br /> I'm curious as to how far it is intended to work. Would that extend to torture? Crippling, unresolved injury that is still ongoing? What about murder, and the Beast player confronts the ghost?<br /> <br /> What does that really consist of, beyond being able to make social maneuvering checks once per day? Is the NPC (or even PC) compelled to actually forgive them for what they did, or is it just &quot;sees them in the best possible light&quot;?<br /> <br /> ~<br /> Second, Be My Guest allows someone to enter a Lair the same way the Beast can. Are they able to leave it to go to any given destination in the same way? That seems to be the read I'm getting, but I'm not sure. Hold the Door clearly specifies that their guest can only leave by the one particular method they entered, I know.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, there's no range on where a Lair can open, can it? Like if you enter in San Francisco, you could land yourself in New York.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:02:10-07:00","id":879774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest#post879761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, Be My Guest allows someone to enter a Lair the same way the Beast can. Are they able to leave it to go to any given destination in the same way? That seems to be the read I'm getting, but I'm not sure. Hold the Door clearly specifies that their guest can only leave by the one particular method they entered, I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication does seem to be that someone authorized to come and go from the Beast's Lair can open a Pathway there using the same correspondences \u2014 the primary limitation being\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of, there's no range on where a Lair can open, can it? Like if you enter in San Francisco, you could land yourself in New York. </div> </div> </div>\u2026the only way you're not eating massive penalties is if your patron has either established their racket in the outside location you're trying to get to or made a Chamber out of an exact facsimile of that location.<br /> <br /> If you were going between two identical houses in San Francisco and New York or two similar houses where your Begotten sponsor has effectively spawned a free-floating Chamber anyway (or if they were present when you made both of those Chambers), that's more likely to work out without complication, but stretching the connection is more likely to just break your buddy's Lair for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:24:32-07:00","id":879786,"title":"","content":"Answer the first, as I understand it: basically, you're preternaturally better at interacting with your prey than a normal human being. However, I think, this merely translates to of characters being more willing to hear the Begotten out than anything else, which, in of itself, does not preclude the target weighing past experiences with the character in deciding how to respond, which an ST could simulate by imposing penalties on that interval's Opening Doors roll, based on how bad that deed was.<br /> <br /> Answer the second: not exactly, beyond the Guest's ability to translate between dimensions. A mundane human is more than likely screwed one way or the other entering the Hive/Lair anyway, so venturing out into the Primordial Dream would not improve their situation much at all. Now, a Werewolf or Mage Guest, on the other hand, is a bit better equipped to handle taking the proverbial long way home, with Sin-Eaters and Lost being less so. <br /> <br /> Lastly, sure, although the accuracy of using it to travel is predicated on the character's experience, so having a Chamber at least narratively similar to your desired destination would make that easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:26:13-07:00","id":879788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=879774#post879774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The implication does seem to be that someone authorized to come and go from the Beast's Lair can open a Pathway there using the same correspondences \u2014 the primary limitation being\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026the only way you're not eating massive penalties is if your patron has either established their racket in the outside location you're trying to get to or made a Chamber out of an exact facsimile of that location.<br /> <br /> If you were going between two identical houses in San Francisco and New York or two similar houses where your Begotten sponsor has effectively spawned a free-floating Chamber anyway (or if they were present when you made both of those Chambers), that's more likely to work out without complication, but stretching the connection is more likely to just break your buddy's Lair for a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sponsors? Patrons? What are you on about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:28:21-07:00","id":879790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=879788#post879788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sponsors? Patrons? What are you on about?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you'd like to share a better concise term for &quot;a Beast character who has authorized you to access their Lair for an indefinite period of time via Be My Guest,&quot; well, be my guest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:42:38-07:00","id":879801,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:53:27-07:00","id":879805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=879774#post879774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The implication does seem to be that someone authorized to come and go from the Beast's Lair can open a Pathway there using the same correspondences \u2014 the primary limitation being\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026the only way you're not eating massive penalties is if your patron has either established their racket in the outside location you're trying to get to or made a Chamber out of an exact facsimile of that location.<br /> <br /> If you were going between two identical houses in San Francisco and New York or two similar houses where your Begotten sponsor has effectively spawned a free-floating Chamber anyway (or if they were present when you made both of those Chambers), that's more likely to work out without complication, but stretching the connection is more likely to just break your buddy's Lair for a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, obviously it's predicated on being able to eat said penalties!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T03:05:50-07:00","id":880009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=879790#post879790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you'd like to share a better concise term for &quot;a Beast character who has authorized you to access their Lair for an indefinite period of time via Be My Guest,&quot; well, be my guest.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about host?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T06:31:47-07:00","id":880112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest#post879761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Alien Allure's Normal effect, how far does it go?<br /> <br /> It indicates that (aside from Heroes) one can harm someone and yet the next day receive a Good Impression, and &quot;all is forgiven.&quot;<br /> I'm curious as to how far it is intended to work. Would that extend to torture? Crippling, unresolved injury that is still ongoing? What about murder, and the Beast player confronts the ghost?</div> </div> </div> </div> The power specifically says that &quot;all is forgiven,&quot; and I take that literally. If you torture a mortal, I turn that mortal into a Hero in responce. As far as I'm concerned, &quot;heroes&quot; are just hunters, and anything that would create a hunter from any other game instead creates a hero for Beast. But if the mortal doesn't become a hero? Then, yeah, they'd forgive no matter what. <br /> <br /> For other supernaturals? Well, its mind control. They like you because of Family, no matter what you do. There's fiction that talks about how one Beast killed another Begotten's biological sibling, and all was forgiven. That's Alien Allure in action, as far as I'm concerned. Mind you, Majesty 1 in VtR has a similar effect - it doesn't change Impressions, but you can beat someone to death while Awe is up, you can torture someone, and you won't get any penalty even from the victim for it. &quot;All is forgiven&quot; is completely within the scope of 2e's power levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does that really consist of, beyond being able to make social maneuvering checks once per day? Is the NPC (or even PC) compelled to actually forgive them for what they did, or is it just &quot;sees them in the best possible light&quot;? </div> </div> </div> Impressions are literally one character's impression of another. If you have a Good Impression, then you think well of someone. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, Be My Guest allows someone to enter a Lair the same way the Beast can. Are they able to leave it to go to any given destination in the same way? That seems to be the read I'm getting, but I'm not sure. Hold the Door clearly specifies that their guest can only leave by the one particular method they entered, I know. </div> </div> </div> I lean on the whole &quot;finding the right burrow&quot; angle here. Every chamber has a real world equivalent, and I'd say you exit there. You want to exit somewhere else, find the right burrow. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T10:20:15-07:00","id":880267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=880009#post880009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about host?</div> </div> </div> </div>Connotations fit Hold The Door more, given that any double meaning that might've been present is obviated by the ability to reflexively rescind the permission. Be My Guest is more like having a supernatural landlord, except you don't need to pay rent or check in with any regularity and they can remotely scrub your keycard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T23:49:05-07:00","id":880777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=880112#post880112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I'm concerned, &quot;heroes&quot; are just hunters</div> </div> </div> </div>That's - well, if you're taking your &quot;rules exactly as written&quot; approach, then that's not only wrong, it's explicitly denied in the material.<br /> If anything, Heroes are much, much closer to Beasts themselves than humans. I would probably consider it legit for a Hero to BECOME a Beast under the right circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=880112#post880112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power specifically says that &quot;all is forgiven,&quot; and I take that literally. If you torture a mortal, I turn that mortal into a Hero in responce. As far as I'm concerned, &quot;heroes&quot; are just hunters, and anything that would create a hunter from any other game instead creates a hero for Beast. But if the mortal doesn't become a hero? Then, yeah, they'd forgive no matter what.<br /> <br /> For other supernaturals? Well, its mind control. They like you because of Family, no matter what you do. There's fiction that talks about how one Beast killed another Begotten's biological sibling, and all was forgiven. That's Alien Allure in action, as far as I'm concerned. Mind you, Majesty 1 in VtR has a similar effect - it doesn't change Impressions, but you can beat someone to death while Awe is up, you can torture someone, and you won't get any penalty even from the victim for it. &quot;All is forgiven&quot; is completely within the scope of 2e's power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Majesty lasts for the scene, and says you can talk yourself out of &quot;minor criminal offenses.&quot;<br /> I'm trying to imagine a situation in which Alien Allure has any real flaw if we take the &quot;all is forgiven&quot; part as absolutely part of the mechanics in the extreme sense suggested there.<br /> I mean, if we take it exactly as you said there - no matter what, Alien Allure means that you can approach anyone, of any bent, and they are compelled to like you, with no resistance check. Awe also lacks an associated dice pool and there's no defense against it (aside from resisting it with your Predatory Aura, another weakness it has that Alien Allure doesn't, aside from Heroes.)<br /> The only way you can then become vulnerable to them is to initiate some sort of offensive action, even if you have a long history of violent sociopathy, and god help you if you can't finish them off within the span of a day. Near as I can figure, the ST shouldn't even allow characters like Mage to mount a Mind effect on themselves, because they shouldn't register anything as wrong.<br /> <br /> Though it's pretty low on the list of Arbitrary ST Crap, having a Beast villain screw with the PCs while they sit, frustrated, unable to do anything about it would be perfectly within the purview of this atavism from that understanding. By the same token, a Beast character with this could walk into a Seers of the Throne meeting and just chill out.<br /> <br /> I can't tell if that's intentional, or if I'm just making too much out of a single sentence of fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 05-03-2016, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T01:23:38-07:00","id":880807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=880777#post880777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no matter what, Alien Allure means that you can approach anyone, of any bent, and they are compelled to like you, with no resistance check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's correct. Like any Atavism, you have to activate it reflexively for the effect to take place, but that's not really a strong barrier to effectiveness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:40:32-07:00","id":880896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=880777#post880777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's - well, if you're taking your &quot;rules exactly as written&quot; approach, then that's not only wrong, it's explicitly denied in the material.<br /> If anything, Heroes are much, much closer to Beasts themselves than humans. I would probably consider it legit for a Hero to BECOME a Beast under the right circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're twisting what I said and putting words in my mouth. I find that very distasteful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm trying to imagine a situation in which Alien Allure has any real flaw if we take the &quot;all is forgiven&quot; part as absolutely part of the mechanics in the extreme sense suggested there.<br /> I mean, if we take it exactly as you said there - no matter what, Alien Allure means that you can approach anyone, of any bent, and they are compelled to like you, with no resistance check. </div> </div> </div> Sure. Its MIND CONTROL. That's what mind control does. Compel and cooerce people to do things they normally wouldn't.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;flaws?&quot; There are a multitude. For one? Alien Allure is actually pretty crappy in terms of mind control. The whole &quot;all is forgiven&quot; thing just sets the Impression to Good, and that's only if you encounter the Beast again; you can't actually get the person to do anything. No, you still need to Social Maneuver the person. The Impression is also not locked at Good - if the Beast shows up and slanders the character, then Impression will drop like a rock. And just because you've forgiven something doesn't mean you've forgotten either - people will take past actions into account, even if they'll forgive you for them. Unlike Awe, if a Beast acts innappropriately, there are immediate short term consequences and social penalties. And potentially long term ones if you do something criminal, because a Good Impression tends to plumbet when crime is involved.<br /> <br /> Just because you have a Good Impression of someone doesn't mean that an antagonistic supernatural suddenly abandons their aspirations, goals, drives, morals and responcibilities. It doesn't mean that they'll sit down and listen to a PC (or NPC) with Alien Allure. It doesn't mean they won't prioritize existing Conditions or fear of breaking points.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if you give an NPC Alien Allure? Its not going to wipe away the reasons that PCs are going after the Beast NPC. Even revenge still holds valid, since that's actually a way to feed your Hunger, something that takes priority for the Begotten. And PCs are generally not targetted by Social Maneuvering - at worst, the party would have a Condition on them. And remember that Social Maneuvering IS NOT mind control. There are things that you just can't convince someone of. Good Impressions does not stop a party of PCs from doing what they feel is necessary or morally right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the same token, a Beast character with this could walk into a Seers of the Throne meeting and just chill out. </div> </div> </div> Chilling with Seers is the game working as intended WITHOUT Alien Allure. That's kind of what the game, as a whole, is meant to do. In fact, by nature, Beasts actually encourage supernaturals they become Kin with to become more and more &quot;dark side.&quot; For mages, that means acting more and more like a Seer. For vampires, its encouraging behavior the strix would approve of. For werewolves, its becoming further away from the Flesh and prioritzing Spirit much like the Pure do, though its unlikely that we'd start adopting Pure Tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can't tell if that's intentional, or if I'm just making too much out of a single sentence of fluff. </div> </div> </div> I think you're reading too much into things that were neither intended nor stated. I also think you mistake how Social Maneuvering works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-03-2016, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T00:04:27-07:00","id":882622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=880112#post880112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The power specifically says that &quot;all is forgiven,&quot; and I take that literally. If you torture a mortal, I turn that mortal into a Hero in responce. As far as I'm concerned, &quot;heroes&quot; are just hunters, and anything that would create a hunter from any other game instead creates a hero for Beast. But if the mortal doesn't become a hero? Then, yeah, they'd forgive no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div> Heroes are not Hunters. They do not come about because a human experienced a Breaking Point and the cause was a Beast, so instead of taking up the Vigil they become Gaston. The corebook goes to great lengths to explain how Beasts and Heroes are related.<br /> <br /> I personally take this a step further and believe that Heroes 'are' Beasts, they're simply in denial. This is hinted at in the corebook with Melanie AKA Sleeping Beauty. It also fits nicely into the narrative of Heroes being bigot figures that have shallow dreams. This is also why Heroes have Legend and Life, just like a Beast, and not Virtue/Vice.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For other supernaturals? Well, its mind control. They like you because of Family, no matter what you do. There's fiction that talks about how one Beast killed another Begotten's biological sibling, and all was forgiven. That's Alien Allure in action, as far as I'm concerned. </div> </div> </div>I don't agree that this was an example of Alien Allure, and I will try to explain why as best I can.<br /> <br /> If Alien Allure were involved the narrator of the story would understand why it happened the way it did. &quot;He's just that way, you can't escape it.&quot; But they don't, they express confusion about it. What we do know is that they are in a deeply involved relationship and then have a fight, and the boyfriend takes it out on the sister. We can assume the other party has some feeling for them?<br /> <br /> Except, Beasts don't have a governing morality that drives them. They lack Humanity, Wisdom, Harmony, Integrity, etc. The only thing that drives them is their Satiety, their hunger. If they have a morality it is arbitrarily tacked on by virtue of their uprbinging and their Life, as soon as that Life goes away they lose what little they have left. It's tenuous. Add to this that they were in a very fucked up relationship from the get go, and that the sister was likely a Mortal.<br /> <br /> A Beast feels family relations to anything that is a monster like them. They don't feel the same way about humans. Let's say I am a Beast, and I'm raised by a human family where there is so much distance between us that I consider them 'my foster family'. This doesn't mean I care nothing about them or their wellbeing, the boyfriend likely wouldn't have killed them in a fit if I didn't, but even if I think my 'foster mom' was an all around okay person, I don't feel the same connections a normal human being would feel for their actual human family. We have a fight about how pulling that is not an okay way to get what you want, and isn't cool. A few weeks later when I feel he's learned that 'lesson' we get back together. It's hard to stay mad about someone dying when you are not overly attached to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind you, Majesty 1 in VtR has a similar effect - it doesn't change Impressions, but you can beat someone to death while Awe is up, you can torture someone, and you won't get any penalty even from the victim for it. &quot;All is forgiven&quot; is completely within the scope of 2e's power levels. </div> </div> </div>Majesty 1 removes all social penalties for Social Manuevers, and nowhere does it say 'even to the victim while you are hurting them'. It says after killing someone. If you are attacking someone you are in physical combat and social manuevering is long gone. Social Manuevering on average will require actions over a long period of time. Especially because Majesty 1 does not boost your Impression level. It doesn't prevent the person from defending themselves in combat, either. For that you need to Enthrall them, or Majesty 5. Majesty and Alien Allure are vastly different if you actually think about it. <br /> Majesty is significantly more powerful than Alien Allure because it can be dispelled, and because after the initial Awe, it requires actual contested rolls to inflict people with conditions that they can gain Beats from. Also - Majesty 1 gives a bonus to Presence, not Manipulation. It will not help you sweet talk someone beyond the initial removed social penalty. It will help you socially dominate someone, though. It'll help you intimidate cops after robbing a bank, but it won't fetch you a positive modifier on Manipulating them into giving up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Impressions are literally one character's impression of another. If you have a Good Impression, then you think well of someone. </div> </div> </div>Impressions serve to designate a period of time that needs to transpire between Social Manuevering rolls. I don't even like it being called 'Impressions' when that's seriously all it does. It's disengenous because being on Good Terms with someone means you should get a positive modifier to get what you want in the first place, right? Or perhaps even fewer doors. <br /> <br /> Alien Allure doesn't do that.<br /> <br /> Let me explain it differently.<br /> <br /> Alien Allure shouldn't do that, because Alien Allure is - pardon the cartoon reference - Ursula getting a chance to manipulate anyone she wants even though she's surrounded by the deformed bodies of those who bothered making a deal with her in the past. It's someone you already know is a villain, but you can't help but hear them out anyway. In that way it's almost every Disney villain ever. <br /> <br /> Alien Allure does not mean that someone likes or adores you. It only adds dice to rolls where your appearance is the driving force behind things. This does not include sealing the deal. It doesn't include anything really beyond making them want to come over and see what's so interesting about you. Low Satiety makes them Charmed the way a Daeva does, but again only at Low Satiety, only if you open every one of those doors, and if you dramatically fail? They automatically become Hostile to you for the rest of the chapter because you pushed it too far. They saw through the bait and got a look at the hook it's attached to. <br /> <br /> Alien Allure will not make someone like you, it won't necessarily make them more likely to accept what you want (The Fame or Status helps, but that's because they feel important, it has nothing to do with your actual likeability). What Alien Allure does guarentee - is that anyone who isn't the Hero will listen to what you have to say, even his beloved girl friend.<br /> <br /> And gosh, after hearing you talk for awhile, if you succeed, it does start to make sense, doesn't it? He really never cared about me, at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:01:27-07:00","id":882713,"title":"","content":"I don't understand why there's such a strong resistance to believing that the Atavism does exactly what it says.<br /> <br /> You can do whatever you want, and it will explicitly be forgiven. The victim will explicitly have a good impression of you afterwards. All of this is spelled out in the Atavism. It's not complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T03:16:50-07:00","id":882722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=882713#post882713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why there's such a strong resistance to believing that the Atavism does exactly what it says.<br /> <br /> You can do whatever you want, and it will explicitly be forgiven. The victim will explicitly have a good impression of you afterwards. All of this is spelled out in the Atavism. It's not complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then it doesn't feel like you're trying very hard.<br /> <br /> First, the book has some of the worst editing of any CoD book I've read, and I've read all of them. It contradicts itself constantly, and this is especially true with Alien Allure where the mechanics <i>do not support</i> the claim that 'all is forgiven' in the Normal effect. You don't even get to ignore any social penalties unless you spent a point of Satiety, and if we're going to continue to use Vampire as precedent, egregious past actions are measured through penalties to your social roll. Difficulty of what you are asking for is measured by your doors. The <i>only</i> thing Alien Allure does is force the other party to hear you out, instead of stone walling with Hostile. Oh, right. It also makes you prettier and appear more impressive than you actually are.<br /> <br /> Players do not like when a form of social manipulation exists that does not have a potential resistance, and affects how their character feels about someone or something (potentially another player. For those of us who ST large moderated chat games? Almost <i>always</i> another player.) Majesty 1 toes this line. The saving grace is that other vampires can buck it, and that all of the following powers have rolls that can be contested and resisted. Forcing a feeling or conclusion onto a player without them having a say or a roll is bad design space.<br /> <br /> Happily, Alien Allure's mechanics don't support the silly flowery language added at the end of the sentence. All it does is force the person to hear you out. Impressions don't give you a positive bonus to your actual social roll, they don't lower the number of doors you have to open, and it doesn't mind control the person into doing whatever you want.<br /> <br /> So, for all of those reasons, I don't understand why we're so hellbent on making an Atavism bend over backwards into negative design space over a single sentence that doesn't reflect the mechanics in a terribly flawed book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T07:27:25-07:00","id":882847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=882622#post882622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes are not Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;As far as I'm concerned.&quot; As in, my opinion. It amazes me how people go out of their way to tell others how they're doing-it-wrong.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I personally take this a step further and believe that Heroes 'are' Beasts, they're simply in denial. </div> </div> </div> It also amazes me how people jump right into their own non-cannical views right after dismissing someone else's. Sure, its one possibility, but its not a given, and lacks support beyond one NPC that acts outside the bounds of what any Hero, Beast, or goetic involved in the Astral should rightfully be able to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Alien Allure were involved the narrator of the story would understand why it happened the way it did. </div> </div> </div> The narrator was an in-character vampire observer. Hardly the most knowledgable narrator who will explicitly spell things out in game mechanics. But you're free to to your opinion on that count, as am I.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Majesty 1 </div> </div> </div> I brought Vampire up entirely as a comparison of what the general power level is across all gamelines. If people can forgive murder in front of their faces on top of a host of other abilities, then its not unbelievable that &quot;all is forgiven&quot; after 24 hours is outside of 2e's increase in power level from 1e. Anything else about what Awe can or cannot do belongs in the Vampire forums. This is not the place to nitpick over vampire abilities, nor does such discussion have any impact on what Alien Allure can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Impressions serve to designate a period of time that needs to transpire between Social Manuevering rolls. I don't even like it being called 'Impressions' when that's seriously all it does. It's disengenous because being on Good Terms with someone means you should get a positive modifier to get what you want in the first place, right? Or perhaps even fewer doors. </div> </div> </div> Its called Impression because its literally an impression. The CofD isn't a system where you strip everything down to numbers and ignore all the words you don't like. The story is the mechanics. Take a look at Thicker Than Water - the reason why Beasts have a Good first impression with supernaturals not for faster rolls, but &quot;allaying the natural fear and suspicions that many supernatural beings have when they\u2019re approached by someone they don\u2019t know who also seems to know their big secret,&quot; (BtP p88).<br /> <br /> This is consistant throughout all the books and preview pdfs we have out for 2e. The Vinculum, certain kiths and Contracts, Cunning Dominance, etc. Going up and down on the Impression chart is irrevocably tied to how the characters are viewed and feelings towards one another. Trying to strip that is inconsistant with how the books portray Impressions as a mechanic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alien Allure doesn't do that. </div> </div> </div> Sure it does. You just don't want it to. You're trying to strip all meaning away from mechanics<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alien Allure does not mean that someone likes or adores you. </div> </div> </div> Nor does having a good impression (both the mechanic and mundane definition). A Good Impression doesn't automatically yield automatic goodwill and peace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It only adds dice to rolls where your appearance is the driving force behind things. This does not include sealing the deal. It doesn't include anything really beyond making them want to come over and see what's so interesting about you. </div> </div> </div> And making it so that &quot;all is forgiven.&quot; If the Beast hurt someone, they can come back with a Good Impression the next day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Low Satiety makes them Charmed the way a Daeva does, but again only at Low Satiety, only if you open every one of those doors, and if you dramatically fail? They automatically become Hostile to you for the rest of the chapter because you pushed it too far. They saw through the bait and got a look at the hook it's attached to. </div> </div> </div> No, they become Hostile to you for a day, after which they reset to Good, as per the exact wording of Alien Allure. You always start with a Good Impression when using the Social Maneuvering system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alien Allure will not make someone like you, it won't necessarily make them more likely to accept what you want (The Fame or Status helps, but that's because they feel important, it has nothing to do with your actual likeability). </div> </div> </div> The bonus to social rolls does say that targets will find you more attractive and more likely to accept what you want. That's kind of why they exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=882722#post882722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it doesn't feel like you're trying very hard.</div> </div> </div> </div> You don't need to try hard to take things at face value. That's kind of the point. I, and others, feel that the power does exaclty what it says on the tin. I personally feel like people don't like the power and are trying to &quot;fix&quot; it when its working as intended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It contradicts itself constantly, and this is especially true with Alien Allure where the mechanics <i>do not support</i> the claim that 'all is forgiven' in the Normal effect. You don't even get to ignore any social penalties unless you spent a point of Satiety, </div> </div> </div> Umm.... where exactly are there contradictions? I don't see any with this Atavism. Please give concrete examples.<br /> <br /> Futhermore, the &quot;ignores penalties&quot; part refers entirely to Forcing Doors. When you Force Doors, you take a penalty equal to the remaining Doors to open. Satiety expendature negates some to all of those penalties. This has nothing to do with the &quot;all is forgiven.&quot; Even if we say that you can ignore penalties from beyond just the number of doors, then we can also say that we can ignore penalties from things like being covered in blood, wearing inappropriate clothing, using an untrained skill, and more. Not something any other part of Alien Allure power does. As well, the removing penalties only happens when Forcing Doors, not soft Maneuvering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Players do not like when a form of social manipulation exists that does not have a potential resistance, and affects how their character feels about someone or something (potentially another player. For those of us who ST large moderated chat games? </div> </div> </div> Alright. Here's the problem. One, if players don't like resistances? <i>Then don't use Social Maneuvering on them. </i>Its right there in the book that the S.M. system is intended for use on NPCs, not PCs. So, don't use it on the PCs if its a problem. If you have players that aren't comfortable with others using mind control on each other, then that should be a conversation you have outside the game. Mind control abilities are something every game has; if PvP is a problem with your group, the problem likely isn't the game, but the players.<br /> <br /> Two, chat games are an overwhelming minority of games and players out there. The rules are designed for table top (including virtual table tops) that bosts around 3-5 players, not massive player populations. Anyone who's ever played in a chat game will tell you that rules don't translate perfectly from one style to the other. So, its meaningless to complain about chat games when you are not the primary audience.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, for all of those reasons, I don't understand why we're so hellbent on making an Atavism bend over backwards into negative design space over a single sentence that doesn't reflect the mechanics in a terribly flawed book. </div> </div> </div> One, don't insult the book or the writers. Two, its only your opinion that anything is negative or flawed; if you don't like the book, then don't play it, but don't shit on it for others. Three, I think you have a mistaken grasp of the mechanics rather than the game itself being the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-05-2016, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:39:32-07:00","id":882990,"title":"","content":"An ability that automatically, irresistibly, and irrevocably allows you to run roughshod over other characters is bad design. Mind magic makes you force a roll, Majesty is deeply limited, the Vinculum needs you to feed the other party (who can't be supernatural anyway).<br /> <br /> ST moderated chats would instantly devolve into a true nightmare if they didn't do exactly what were saying - make it so that the &quot;all is forgiven&quot; line means only that you will hear the other party out.<br /> If we go it your way, Alien Allure becomes one of the most powerful single abilities in the entire lineup, by virtue of the fact that it has no weaknesses, no resistance, and you can't even defend yourself by saying you'll open fire the moment they show up or muster a defense. There is no plausible way another PC could do ANYTHING about a Beast with this power if we take your extreme viewpoint - unless the ST decided that they could by disabling Social Maneuvering, which, hey, most of us do for PCs anyway, right?<br /> NPCs are just hosed.<br /> <br /> I find it difficult to believe that they would put something that busted into a series where they've clearly worked so hard to limit abuse, so I figure it was never intended to go that far.<br /> <br /> An editor/developer is free to correct me on that, maybe lay out a little nuance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 05-05-2016, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:10:37-07:00","id":883149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=882847#post882847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;As far as I'm concerned.&quot; As in, my opinion. It amazes me how people go out of their way to tell others how they're doing-it-wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>The OP of this thread was asking for help interpreting the book. I apologize if I offended you, but I assumed you were also trying to help them interpret what is in the book.<br /> <br /> At no point did I say you are running your games wrong if that's the way you do it. If you are posing an interpretation of the book to help someone else who specifically asked for help interpreting the book - then you are doing it wrong? Because the book mentions again and again and again that Heroes and Hunters are not even close to the same thing. This is one of the things it is consistent on, denying that connection denies the themes between those two forces. This wouldn't be a bad thing if you explained why you feel that's for the best. All I can ascertain is that you do it as a form of punishment, but to my eyes reckless behavior is its own disadvantage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also amazes me how people jump right into their own non-cannical views right after dismissing someone else's. Sure, its one possibility, but its not a given, and lacks support beyond one NPC that acts outside the bounds of what any Hero, Beast, or goetic involved in the Astral should rightfully be able to do. </div> </div> </div>Look, if you're going to post your views on an important element of the game, you're absolutely welcome to do so. If you post your ideas in a public forum then you are allowing for the possibility that those ideas come under scrutiny. You're welcome to challenge my ideas, but &quot;You attacked my views so you don't get to share your own without being a hypocrite!&quot; is not a valid criticism.<br /> <br /> Since you are claiming that my interpretation of the canon is in some way equivalent to your outright rejecting the canon. I can address that, for sure.<br /> <br /> As I already mentioned there is support for it in the canon because there is an NPC where that is expressed. That is precedent, that makes it possible. That is an endorsement via the book that this connection is in keeping with the themes behind what Beasts and Heroes are. Heroes have Legend and Life, Hunters do not. Heroes touch the Primordial Dream, Hunters do not. Often, especially in the original write up, Heroes emerge from people close to the Beast, friends and family.<br /> <br /> The difference here is substantial. If you value the Heroes are Hunters model as a way of punishing your players for heinous acts, then that\u2019s wonderful as long as you feel it enriches your games. It doesn\u2019t mean people on the internet are going to just quietly accept that in a thread about interpreting the book, though.<br /> <br /> Also, it\u2019s not cool to run around claiming that people are intentionally twisting your words to have a go at you, when misunderstanding is far more likely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The narrator was an in-character vampire observer. Hardly the most knowledgable narrator who will explicitly spell things out in game mechanics. But you're free to to your opinion on that count, as am I. </div> </div> </div>How does that change things at all? If Alien Allure were involved, and applied in the manner you suggest it should, the vampire would be just as subjected to it and it would make no sense for them to be confused and out of the picture. Please explain how your interpretation is more solid in light of that, instead of just saying \u2018Believe whatever you want.\u2019<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I brought Vampire up entirely as a comparison of what the general power level is across all gamelines. If people can forgive murder in front of their faces on top of a host of other abilities, then its not unbelievable that &quot;all is forgiven&quot; after 24 hours is outside of 2e's increase in power level from 1e. Anything else about what Awe can or cannot do belongs in the Vampire forums. This is not the place to nitpick over vampire abilities, nor does such discussion have any impact on what Alien Allure can do. </div> </div> </div>So you\u2019re allowed to bring up Vampire in the Beast forum, but I\u2019m not allowed to dissect your point? Excuse me? You want to play the hypocrisy card? Don\u2019t you ever tell me what I can and cannot confront you over. You brought up Awe, compared it to Alien Allure, this thread is exactly the place to nitpick your comparison.<br /> <br /> Awe does not do what Alien Allure does, it does not have the same fluff - nowhere - does it say that you are forgiven. The person is so focused on you they can\u2019t even think about the person you just killed. They have to roll Wits + Composure just to look past them.<br /> <br /> You want to defend your point? Fucking defend it, instead of calling \u20181, 2, 3, we\u2019re not in the Vampire forum so bases all over me!~\u2019<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its called Impression because its literally an impression. The CofD isn't a system where you strip everything down to numbers and ignore all the words you don't like. The story is the mechanics. Take a look at Thicker Than Water - the reason why Beasts have a Good first impression with supernaturals not for faster rolls, but &quot;allaying the natural fear and suspicions that many supernatural beings have when they\u2019re approached by someone they don\u2019t know who also seems to know their big secret,&quot; (BtP p88). </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I know about Thicker than Water.<br /> <br /> I also know that it repeatedly stresses that this does not mean they are actually friendly to you. It does not make them more likely to listen, and depending on the circumstances of your meeting it could also not even matter. What is the value of calling it \u2018a good impression\u2019 when in reality all it\u2019s doing is ensuring the other person has to hear you out? (all else being equal)<br /> <br /> I guess I don\u2019t get to pick and choose the passages I want, but you get to do so, first with Heroes and then with an ability that boosts impression \u2018for the sake of Social Maneuvering only\u2019. The book fails to sell me on the notion that Impressions are anything but an arbitrary name they slapped onto a mechanic that needed a name, only for them to have to go out of their way that future abilities that modify it only do so \u2018for the purposes of Social Maneuvering.\u2019 The most literal interpretation of Thicker than Water is that a Prince is going to hear you out, but he doesn\u2019t have to like you. He doesn\u2019t have to lower his standards for doing what you want. He might even directly oppose you.<br /> <br /> How does that translate in any meaningful way to someone making a good impression at a job interview? With a person at the bar? Etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is consistant throughout all the books and preview pdfs we have out for 2e. The Vinculum, certain kiths and Contracts, Cunning Dominance, etc. Going up and down on the Impression chart is irrevocably tied to how the characters are viewed and feelings towards one another. Trying to strip that is inconsistant with how the books portray Impressions as a mechanic. </div> </div> </div>Except for all of the reasons I listed above - it\u2019s not. The more supernatural powers get involved the more the CoD games have shown that Impression has nothing to do with whether or not the person likes you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nor does having a good impression (both the mechanic and mundane definition). A Good Impression doesn't automatically yield automatic goodwill and peace. </div> </div> </div>The mundane definition of a Good Impression doesn\u2019t engender goodwill and peace? What the fuck are you talking about? From Mechanic perspective Impression does engender peace - in that they have to listen to you - it doesn\u2019t engender goodwill, and you just got done saying that it does earlier in your posts. Forgiveness is goodwill. If you have a Good Impression at an interview - you just engendered goodwill. So I am not sure where your understanding of mundane good impressions comes from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, they become Hostile to you for a day, after which they reset to Good, as per the exact wording of Alien Allure. You always start with a Good Impression when using the Social Maneuvering system. </div> </div> </div>Here\u2019s what I actually said: \u201cLow Satiety makes them Charmed the way a Daeva does, but again only at Low Satiety, only if you open every one of those doors, and if you dramatically fail? They automatically become Hostile to you for the rest of the chapter because you pushed it too far. They saw through the bait and got a look at the hook it's attached to.\u201d<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s what the book says: \u201cLow Satiety: Any Social roll involving appearance counts as an exceptional success with three successes or more. Furthermore, so long as she avoids Hard Leverage, opening all Doors imposes the Charmed Condition on the target of her Social maneuvering. However, she sometimes repulses people instead as she slips into the uncanny valley. A dramatic failure changes her impression level to \u201chostile\u201d with that person for the rest of the chapter, and imposes a penalty to Social rolls against that target equal to the Beast\u2019s Lair.\u201d<br /> <br /> Hey look, it says chapter, not one day, in regards to this specific effect that I was talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The bonus to social rolls does say that targets will find you more attractive and more likely to accept what you want. That's kind of why they exist. </div> </div> </div>Are you one of those people that believes Striking Looks applies to every social roll? \u2018Cause that is literally what this is. I already explained the numerous situations where the book has stipulated it doesn\u2019t apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't need to try hard to take things at face value. That's kind of the point. I, and others, feel that the power does exaclty what it says on the tin. I personally feel like people don't like the power and are trying to &quot;fix&quot; it when its working as intended. </div> </div> </div>And I, having numerous experiences with player vs player games understand why forcing another player to have an emotion reaction without their consent or any possible resistance is bad design space, and that clinging desperately to a portion of a sentence that poorly corresponds to the mechanics of the ability just makes it clear you\u2019re more interested in getting away with whatever you want without consequence for no role, with no possible chance of resistance. Shit, no wonder you want Heroes to pop up like daisies, you need them to rein things in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Umm.... where exactly are there contradictions? I don't see any with this Atavism. Please give concrete examples. </div> </div> </div>I said the book is filled with contradictions. I didn\u2019t narrow it down to one Atavism. I\u2019m also not going to go through the entire book a fourth time listing every time one passage contradicts another. If you didn\u2019t notice the contradictions, the frequent spelling and grammatical errors, and so forth, then you might except that the book is well editted. You\u2019d be wrong, though.<br /> <br /> I already listed the contradictions behind Alien Allure, in every post we\u2019ve talked about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Futhermore, the &quot;ignores penalties&quot; part refers entirely to Forcing Doors. When you Force Doors, you take a penalty equal to the remaining Doors to open. Satiety expendature negates some to all of those penalties. This has nothing to do with the &quot;all is forgiven.&quot; Even if we say that you can ignore penalties from beyond just the number of doors, then we can also say that we can ignore penalties from things like being covered in blood, wearing inappropriate clothing, using an untrained skill, and more. Not something any other part of Alien Allure power does. As well, the removing penalties only happens when Forcing Doors, not soft Maneuvering. </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re right, how does this do anything but strengthen my point? If any social penalties are still there from what you did in the past, then they didn\u2019t very well forgive you, now did they? Anyone who wants revenge for you killing your sister? It\u2019s not going to make them drop their gun and walk away. It does mean that if you can restrain them, they have to listen. They can\u2019t just hide behind their Hostility. The mechanics reflect this, and that\u2019s why saying \u2018the Beast is Forgiven\u2019 is disingenuous as hell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alright. Here's the problem. One, if players don't like resistances? <i>Then don't use Social Maneuvering on them. </i>Its right there in the book that the S.M. system is intended for use on NPCs, not PCs. So, don't use it on the PCs if its a problem. If you have players that aren't comfortable with others using mind control on each other, then that should be a conversation you have outside the game. Mind control abilities are something every game has; if PvP is a problem with your group, the problem likely isn't the game, but the players. </div> </div> </div>Again, some of us run large moderated chats where a large portion of the interaction is between players. If you strip away social maneuvering, then social skills and attributes have no meaning, except for the special occasions where a personal scene is done, or very rarely in larger scenes. The other problem with this is that you could still roll physical skills against another player, and having that player say \u201cYou can\u2019t attack my character because dying isn\u2019t what I want for my character.\u201d doesn\u2019t apply without being asinine.<br /> <br /> \u201cPeople don\u2019t like having no resistance or possible out for a starting level social power that forces the player to portray a specific emotional reaction.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, well then I guess don\u2019t include Social Maneuvering against players. It says as much in the book.\u201d<br /> <br /> Thanks, but that was never the issue, my players are plenty mature enough to handle complex social intrigues that they have to roll with - when their character\u2019s traits, stats, and personality have any effect on the results - moreover, we\u2019re profoundly uncomfortable with the idea that PCs should be some kind of super heroes that ignore any inconvenient effects like your interpretation of Alien Allure, but the NPCs for whatever reason are still vulnerable. If you reach that point, there\u2019s something wrong with the ability itself, and that puts it into poor design space.<br /> <br /> Also according to your interpretation, removing the Social Maneuver system wouldn\u2019t change anything. They\u2019d still have to forgive people with Alien Allure automatically - still without any rolls - and that would still influence them without taking their characters into consideration at all. The only difference is we wouldn\u2019t be using the Social system anymore.<br /> <br /> Unless again, we just make Alien Allure have no effect on PCs, I believe that\u2019s bad design space. You can say \u2018Other games are doing it, too.\u2019 (they\u2019re not) \u2018But that\u2019s what the way the fluff sentence paints it.\u2019 (Who cares? It\u2019s not reflected in the mechanics.)<br /> <br /> But neither of those is an actual argument for why something like that should exist even if they were valid claims.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two, chat games are an overwhelming minority of games and players out there. The rules are designed for table top (including virtual table tops) that bosts around 3-5 players, not massive player populations. Anyone who's ever played in a chat game will tell you that rules don't translate perfectly from one style to the other. So, its meaningless to complain about chat games when you are not the primary audience. </div> </div> </div>I also play in Online Table Tops, and the people in it have the same problem with Alien Allure that Jachra has, the same problem I have, and we don\u2019t support neutering one-third of the games skills and stats for the sake of accommodating a poor design space. If we wanted to play a game where social skills didn\u2019t matter, we\u2019d go play D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One, don't insult the book or the writers. Two, its only your opinion that anything is negative or flawed; if you don't like the book, then don't play it, but don't shit on it for others. Three, I think you have a mistaken grasp of the mechanics rather than the game itself being the problem. </div> </div> </div>1. I never insulted the writers. I criticized the book for being poorly edited. There are spelling mistakes, grammar mistakes, inconsistencies, and fluff that doesn\u2019t match mechanics and implies results that are outrageous. You need to chill out, and stop assuming an attack on your idea is an attack against you. Do you really think I would be arguing if I didn\u2019t value - in some way - what the authors of Beast have created? You think I wasn\u2019t there as soon as the idea was proposed, hungry for it, and inspired by what they were striving for? You don\u2019t know a thing about me, and implying that that I hate the book or its writers for their shortcomings isn\u2019t just twisting my words, it\u2019s jumping to conclusions.<br /> <br /> 2. Arguments are by definition an exchange of opinions, what you\u2019ve said is also an opinion. If you don\u2019t want your opinion to be challenge in an open forum - then don\u2019t post it in an open forum for discussion. The purpose of discourse is to exchange ideas, have those ideas challenged, and then grow as a result. But I am finding it very difficult to stay polite with you when you\u2019re acting like a brat.<br /> <br /> 3. So which is it? Am I forsaking the fluff and cleaving entirely to the mechanics, or do I just plain have the mechanics wrong? Because so far you haven\u2019t eluded to how my understanding of the mechanics has been inaccurate. You\u2019ve rambled about the flavor of the mechanics for no other reason than \u2018well I took this misleading name and ran with it\u2019, and then there\u2019s the other instance where you didn\u2019t even defend your bringing Majesty into this, and attacked me over being so pedantic for dissecting your statement and the ability in question outside of the vampire forum. The other instance involves you calling me out on a mechanics quote that I was correct about in the context of what you were quoting. So far, the only time I slipped up on the mechanics was in applying the removal of social penalties to all rolls, not just rolls using Hard Leveraged. A correction that only served to strengthen my point, because now it doesn\u2019t even remove social penalties from anything other than the Hard Leverage drawback, even <i>if</i> you spend the Satiety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 05-05-2016, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:07:34-07:00","id":883723,"title":"","content":"Oh, this is another discussion about using the book's rules in a format they were never intended. Cool.<br /> <br /> The power works exactly as described, and does exactly what it says, and you're both trying too hard to find excuses to say it doesn't because you're running the game in a way it wasn't designed, and the effects of this Atavism make that difficult. The solution is really simple:<br /> <br /> Houserule it.<br /> <br /> Don't try to make the (very strange) argument that because this complicates the (non-standard) way you decide to run games (online chats, LARPs, whatever) that it must not work that way. Because it does. Explicitly. It would be almost impossible for it to be MORE explicit. It literally says all is forgiven. Full stop. <br /> <br /> Your impression moves to Good. No matter what. (Note that this will also lower impression if it's above 'Good'). That is how the power works. There's no real room for argument, it's how its written. If you don't like it, or if you feel its bad design, or if it makes your job harder, then see above: <b>Those are all great arguments for House-ruling it</b>.<br /> <br /> It's powerful. That's okay. For comparison that's more along the lines of this kind of ridiculous power level in 2E: Any Mage with 5 dots in any Arcana can kill anyone (even supers) with a single success on a single roll. Supers don't even get to use their power stat to defend themselves.<br /> <br /> I imagine you'll want to house rule that for your chats, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-06-2016, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:02:37-07:00","id":883831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=883149#post883149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">) \u2018But that\u2019s what the way the fluff sentence paints it.\u2019 (Who cares? It\u2019s not reflected in the mechanics.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to mention one thing here. Onyx Path has very clearly stated that they do not separate those two concepts. Every word of the book is mechanics. It may not be a subsystem, but it is still mechanics.<br /> <br /> MCN is coming into this with that knowledge; that is why the sentence that 'all is forgiven' is taken as a fact. Any criticisms of the system have to look at it in this light for the developers (and many on these forums) to actually take them seriously.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:16:09-07:00","id":883966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=883723#post883723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, this is another discussion about using the book's rules in a format they were never intended. Cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game was never intended for online tabletop? Cool, I'll bear that in mind when considering one of the kickstarter rewards was to have the lead developer run a game over Skype.<br /> <br /> Or you're just focus firing on my bringing bigger chat games into it as well, as a way of expressing the scale of the problem. That's a fancy strawman you've got there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The power works exactly as described, and does exactly what it says, and you're both trying too hard to find excuses to say it doesn't because you're running the game in a way it wasn't designed, and the effects of this Atavism make that difficult. The solution is really simple: </div> </div> </div>Please tell me how I am not running Beast: the Primordial the way it is designed to be because I didn't take colorful language as gospel. I have reflected every power Alien Allure represents with its mechanics, I've simply never forced an NPC or PC to forgive someone. You could say that in order for a Good Impression to feasibly happen, you <i>have</i> to forgive. Except... No. No you don't. There are plenty of examples of people who should be hostile toward one another, social maneuvering each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Houserule it. </div> </div> </div>Less of a House Rule and more of a clarification to my players, for my part. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't try to make the (very strange) argument that because this complicates the (non-standard) way you decide to run games (online chats, LARPs, whatever) that it must not work that way. Because it does. Explicitly. It would be almost impossible for it to be MORE explicit. It literally says all is forgiven. Full stop. </div> </div> </div>Or you know. Table Top. NPCs can have Alien Allure, too. Having the PCs be immune to that but making the NPCs bend over backwards isn't engaging. If you develop a mechanic that I had to set police tape around, you're entering bad design space. I'm so tired of the 'well it doesn't count, because it wasn't created with Player Characters interacting in mind. Characters are characters. If I wanted one rule for the ruled and another for the rulers, I'd be playing Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your impression moves to Good. No matter what. (Note that this will also lower impression if it's above 'Good'). That is how the power works. There's no real room for argument, it's how its written. If you don't like it, or if you feel its bad design, or if it makes your job harder, then see above: <b>Those are all great arguments for House-ruling it</b> </div> </div> </div>First of all - what? I seriously doubt Atavism's intention is to insure your impression is always 'just good' even if it's usually Excellent or Perfect with that person. Making yourself 'more' alluring shouldn't reduce your place on the table. But I suppose the writers can't be bothered to slip an 'at least Good' in there. So now we should take it as absolute fact that the intention is to lower Impressions/expectations by making... you more alluring. What?<br /> <br /> And of course, welcome back to 'That's your opinion, and you shouldn't be debating the value of it in a public forum devoted to the topic.' I suppose in the future I will post my opinion in response to a thread, and then just never reply to it again because I shouldn't be arguing with others over it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's powerful. That's okay. For comparison that's more along the lines of this kind of ridiculous power level in 2E: Any Mage with 5 dots in any Arcana can kill anyone (even supers) with a single success on a single roll. Supers don't even get to use their power stat to defend themselves. </div> </div> </div>I haven't gotten that far into Mage, I've been spending all of my time writing up a werewolf setting for my tabletop group. But if what you say is true, then yes - I would immediately start house ruling things. Things like that remove difficulty and conflict from the game. When you make an ability that is reflexive, has no roll, and cannot be resisted by any means whatsoever, and this ability forces an emotional response (Even beyond any mechanical rolls, since again, the mechanics of the ability don't support 'forgiveness'. They don't remove social penalties for past actions, they don't reduce doors, and so on.) then that removes conflict, chance and difficulty from the game. That makes for a less compelling story, and that means the developers could have done better.<br /> <br /> Considering Mage was in playtest hell for literally years, I really hope you're exaggerating, but somehow I doubt it at this point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I imagine you'll want to house rule that for your chats, too. </div> </div> </div>Chats, tabletops, you name it. I don't see how the wide spectrum of games I play somehow makes my opinion less valid. <br /> <br /> You're mirroring the argument of 'Too bad, that's what the book says, deal with it or house rule it, but you're wrong.' (to paraphrase) But this discussion asked for clarification on how Alien Allure works. And if it works the way you and MCR believes it to work - then should it work that way? That is the entire focus of the discussion, and responding repeatedly with 'It doesn't matter, that's what the book says. It doesn't matter, full stop.' is not conductive to the subject of whether or not it <i>should</i> work that way in the first place. <br /> <br /> Also, talking about house ruling, if we take the fluff &quot;All is forgiven(.)&quot; literally, because what could be more clear? We already have to start implementing house rules, because that forgiveness would imply you don't suffer the social penalties associated with the things you have forgiven you for. Which the listed mechanics do not cover in any shape or form. Thus you are house ruling the ability if you use it in any sense unless it involves foregoing 'Social Combat' or Social Maneuvers all together. <br /> <br /> And I'd still love to hear why that's a good thing instead of being told for the fourth time that 'It doesn't matter, that's what the book says.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:18:31-07:00","id":883969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=883831#post883831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to mention one thing here. Onyx Path has very clearly stated that they do not separate those two concepts. Every word of the book is mechanics. It may not be a subsystem, but it is still mechanics.<br /> <br /> MCN is coming into this with that knowledge; that is why the sentence that 'all is forgiven' is taken as a fact. Any criticisms of the system have to look at it in this light for the developers (and many on these forums) to actually take them seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanics are the mechanism by which the game tells its stories. I'm not saying you're wrong that they said that, but if fluff = mechanics was a thing that made any sense, we wouldn't be writing up character sheets with skills dots and experience charted. Mechanics exist because fluff cannot balance the system, it cannot clearly and concretely determine the cause of an effect. So if they said that their fluff is also their mechanics, then that's an oxymoron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T13:42:41-07:00","id":884037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, the Beast always starts with a good first impression using the Social maneuvering system. If the Beast has previously caused harm to the target, she must avoid him for at least a day to gain this benefit. When she sees him again, all is forgiven. Heroes are immune to this effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I want to directly state that this entire section of text is listed where the <b>mechanics </b>for the Atavism are listed: Under 'Normal Effect'. The 'fluff' for this atavism, and others, is listed separately, substantially above this section. From this text, we can conclude the following without doubt or question (because these are the rules of the power, listed where the power's rules are):<br /> <br /> 1) All is forgiven when the target of the atavism sees the user again (assuming 'a day' has passed), unless the target is a Hero. This <b>explicitly</b> includes situations where the Beast previously caused harm to the target. There is absolutely <b>no room</b> for doubt or interpretation here. The hypothetical situation of harming someone and then coming back later is <b>the entire point of this section of the text</b>. Seriously. It's there for this exact reason.<br /> 2) The Beast <b>always</b> starts with a good first impression using social maneuvering. There are no exceptions listed for using the ability on someone you were at a higher impression level with, and words like 'Increased to' are avoided. So yes, it 'sets' the impression to Good, regardless of what it was before.<br /> <br /> Ruling otherwise on either of these points is not clarifying the rules. It's making a house rule.<br /> <br /> And that's fine.<br /> <br /> Side Note: No, I wasn't exaggerating about the power level of 2E Mages.<br /> <br /> Edit: This discussion wasn't framed as 'As written, Alien Allure is too powerful for my tastes. What are some good ways to tone it down?'. It was framed as asking for how the rules actually work. My posts are all written from that frame of reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-06-2016, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:44:32-07:00","id":884086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=883969#post883969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mechanics are the mechanism by which the game tells its stories. I'm not saying you're wrong that they said that, but if fluff = mechanics was a thing that made any sense, we wouldn't be writing up character sheets with skills dots and experience charted. Mechanics exist because fluff cannot balance the system, it cannot clearly and concretely determine the cause of an effect. So if they said that their fluff is also their mechanics, then that's an oxymoron.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your argument is arbitrarily throwing away all the subsystems for no reason.<br /> <br /> I said all of the text counts as mechanics. That means that when the book describes Attributes, Skills, and Merits, its mechanics. And when it describes how beasts have semi-prophetic dreams before their Devouring, its mechanics. Note how there is no subsystem for those dreams, they just happen. By standard it would be in the characters backstory but you could play a mortal that turns to a beast or a beast who helps another go through it. Still doesn't have a subsystem, still counts as mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:14:47-07:00","id":884167,"title":"","content":"Alright the way I see the whole alien allure thing is like this. For whatever reason (be it an aura, pheromones, a sort of magnetism, or being able to hold yourself in a certain way) people are naturally attracted to you for the base portion. The same effect makes it hard for them to hold a grudge against you when they're in your presence, provided you've given them sufficient cool down time. Now downside this theoretically means you could torture someone or kill someone else (The victim's forgiveness is slightly irrelevant after they die.) on Friday then meet up with them Monday and despite the shit you pulled they'll have a hard time being angry with you over it when you meet up. Now obviously Heroes are immune to this since they're the natural predator for the beghotten. I can't speak on ghosts since my knowledge of the rules for ghosts in CoD is basically non-existent.<br /> <br /> The way I interpret this though is that it is presence based. The thing is this means your actions still have consequence, so if you torture a person on Friday and then make sure to avoid them Saturday that doesn't mean they might not have skipped town, called the cops, or any of the other rather natural responses to having been tortured recently. Yeah if you can meet up it'll be water under the bridge and they'll probably call off the cops or what have you, but that isn't going to work until you've met up with them. It's kind of like an issue in &quot;Gotham Sirens.&quot; Basically Harley Quinn had spent the run till this point rather pissed off at the Joker for the many many different ways he had wronged her over their relationship. For reasons I don't recall something set her off and she decided to go break into Arkham and kill the Joker. She spent the entire issue working her way to her confrontation where she would do the deed and yet as soon as she met up with him again, she melted, admitted that there was probably something wrong with her, let him loose, and went back to her role as his adoring sidekick. The thing is this doesn't change the context of the previous incidents, she doesn't view them in any sort of positive light, and she doesn't forget about them. Just as soon as they were back together she stopped viewing them as important. That's kind of how I view it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 05-06-2016, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:41:06-07:00","id":884267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=884086#post884086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your argument is arbitrarily throwing away all the subsystems for no reason.<br /> <br /> I said all of the text counts as mechanics. That means that when the book describes Attributes, Skills, and Merits, its mechanics. And when it describes how beasts have semi-prophetic dreams before their Devouring, its mechanics. Note how there is no subsystem for those dreams, they just happen. By standard it would be in the characters backstory but you could play a mortal that turns to a beast or a beast who helps another go through it. Still doesn't have a subsystem, still counts as mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't understand what you mean by 'throwing away the subsystems'. Or how I could be doing it arbitrarily. Fluff and mechanics are not the same thing, if they were the same thing we wouldn't need separate words to delineate what they are. Your example of the dreams is not mechanics, it's fluff. It's imperative to the theme of the game but there are no mechanics telling you how it works or how it must be done. They aren't even unilaterally prophetic. There is an absence of mechanics so that the Storyteller knows to do whatever they think fits best for the story they are trying to tell. It's also entirely possible that it will receive mechanics later on, like vampire dreams in Rites of Spring. <br /> <br /> 'Fluff' fills out the themes and stories the game is supposed to tell. Mechanics are the <i>mechanism</i> by which those stories are told. If a bit of fluff listed in an ability imply one thing, but that thing is not reflected by the actual <i>mechanisms</i> of the ability, then I feel it's an entirely valid interpretation to dismiss the fluff as colorful language to add context to what the ability is doing. <br /> <br /> It's akin to the statement above that Alien Allure should reduce your impression if it was initially higher as soon as you use it. That's not an interpretation. That's taking the book to Peleps Deled levels of &quot;Your first mistake was believing there are interpretations of Beast: the Primordial.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T19:59:49-07:00","id":884282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=884167#post884167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright the way I see the whole alien allure thing is like this. For whatever reason (be it an aura, pheromones, a sort of magnetism, or being able to hold yourself in a certain way) people are naturally attracted to you for the base portion. The same effect makes it hard for them to hold a grudge against you when they're in your presence, provided you've given them sufficient cool down time. Now downside this theoretically means you could torture someone or kill someone else (The victim's forgiveness is slightly irrelevant after they die.) on Friday then meet up with them Monday and despite the shit you pulled they'll have a hard time being angry with you over it when you meet up. Now obviously Heroes are immune to this since they're the natural predator for the beghotten. I can't speak on ghosts since my knowledge of the rules for ghosts in CoD is basically non-existent.<br /> <br /> The way I interpret this though is that it is presence based. The thing is this means your actions still have consequence, so if you torture a person on Friday and then make sure to avoid them Saturday that doesn't mean they might not have skipped town, called the cops, or any of the other rather natural responses to having been tortured recently. Yeah if you can meet up it'll be water under the bridge and they'll probably call off the cops or what have you, but that isn't going to work until you've met up with them. It's kind of like an issue in &quot;Gotham Sirens.&quot; Basically Harley Quinn had spent the run till this point rather pissed off at the Joker for the many many different ways he had wronged her over their relationship. For reasons I don't recall something set her off and she decided to go break into Arkham and kill the Joker. She spent the entire issue working her way to her confrontation where she would do the deed and yet as soon as she met up with him again, she melted, admitted that there was probably something wrong with her, let him loose, and went back to her role as his adoring sidekick. The thing is this doesn't change the context of the previous incidents, she doesn't view them in any sort of positive light, and she doesn't forget about them. Just as soon as they were back together she stopped viewing them as important. That's kind of how I view it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Very good point that, until 24h have passed and the target sees you again...they're going to act appropriately.<br /> <br /> That will likely include doing everything in their power to avoid seeing you again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T20:05:37-07:00","id":884284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=884267#post884267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's akin to the statement above that Alien Allure should reduce your impression if it was initially higher as soon as you use it. That's not an interpretation. That's taking the book to Peleps Deled levels of &quot;Your first mistake was believing there are interpretations of Beast: the Primordial.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>..it's the rules as written, and it makes perfect sense in the context of the power as well. It's 'Alien' Allure. The power goes out of its way several times to clarify that your behavior isn't 'normal'. It comes across as alien enough to knock impressions down to good, just as it's alluring enough to bump them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T03:19:03-07:00","id":884502,"title":"","content":"The way I like to think of it is its like our glorious friend and leader Desus (what a <i>great</i> guy!). You can get everyone to listen to what you have to say, even if they know better.<br /> <br /> Heck, you can even straight up tell someone to murder their family! All you have to do is open all of their Doors and...<br /> <br /> Oh, they just took a Condition instead of doing what you wanted. That's... OK, I guess.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Compare to higher levels of Majesty where &quot;oh, yeah, sure - go ahead and eat my family in front of me&quot; is just what it does. Compare to Werewolf, where you can drop a few Essence and <i>blast</i> through Doors in about a turn. Compare to Mage's &quot;I'll just rewrite your personality kthnxbai&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;People will like you and say you're great in bed even if you aren't (<a href=\"http://oglaf.com/prowess/\" target=\"_blank\">obligatory Oglaf</a>)&quot; is perfectly fine - the &quot;in bed&quot; is metaphorical in this case, even if it isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T04:59:00-07:00","id":884551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=884267#post884267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fluff and mechanics are not the same thing, if they were the same thing we wouldn't need separate words to delineate what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div> They are the same thing in the CofD books, as per Word of God from the writers and developers. This has been mentioned a number of times in the past. Story descriptors of merits and magical powers are not ignorable with these games. That's not how they were designed.<br /> <br /> Also, you are misusing the terms fluff and crunch. Or, by their less offensive and demeaning terms, setting lore and mechanics. Mechanics are everything that directly affects your character, not just raw numbers. If a power says that you feel happy and warm on the inside, that's a mechanic even without a single number attached. That's crunch. Lore / fluff involves things like history, mood settings, and other passive story elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T08:31:14-07:00","id":886295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/879761-question-regarding-alien-allure-and-be-my-guest?p=884267#post884267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't understand what you mean by 'throwing away the subsystems'. Or how I could be doing it arbitrarily. Fluff and mechanics are not the same thing, if they were the same thing we wouldn't need separate words to delineate what they are. Your example of the dreams is not mechanics, it's fluff. It's imperative to the theme of the game but there are no mechanics telling you how it works or how it must be done. They aren't even unilaterally prophetic. There is an absence of mechanics so that the Storyteller knows to do whatever they think fits best for the story they are trying to tell. It's also entirely possible that it will receive mechanics later on, like vampire dreams in Rites of Spring.<br /> <br /> 'Fluff' fills out the themes and stories the game is supposed to tell. Mechanics are the <i>mechanism</i> by which those stories are told. If a bit of fluff listed in an ability imply one thing, but that thing is not reflected by the actual <i>mechanisms</i> of the ability, then I feel it's an entirely valid interpretation to dismiss the fluff as colorful language to add context to what the ability is doing.<br /> <br /> It's akin to the statement above that Alien Allure should reduce your impression if it was initially higher as soon as you use it. That's not an interpretation. That's taking the book to Peleps Deled levels of &quot;Your first mistake was believing there are interpretations of Beast: the Primordial.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was reffering to this &quot;<i>but if fluff = mechanics was a thing that made any sense, we wouldn't be writing up character sheets with skills dots and experience charted&quot;</i>. Where you imply that if there was no seperation we wouldn't have character sheets. That is a fallacy, you are throwing out the subsystems in order to make your point. Health is a subsystem, combat is a subsystem, Social Manuevering is a subsystem. Some mechanics are subsytems, some arne't. They are just the way the game works with no special system for it.<br /> <br /> 'Mechanics are the <i>mechanism</i> by which those stories are told' true, but that doesn't mean they have to use numbers and keywords, or be separated by different formatting. This is a storytelling game and thus everything in the book is there to serve the storytelling of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:28:27-07:00","id":889440,"title":"","content":"Impression level only changes the interval between attempts to open doors. The step of social maneuvering where the ST applies an impression level to the npc happens after the step where he decides if the attempt is possible at all. <br /> If the goal of your social is deemed unrealistic by the ST It doesn't matter if your impression level is good or hostile or if you have alien allure. The social maneuvering ends before impression level gets assigned. <br /> <br /> Impression level doesn't make it more likely that you can influence someone anyway. It just let's you know whether you succeed or fail faster. <br /> <br /> Beasts can play with impression levels without resistance because impression has very little impact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}